SU(1)                       User Commands

NAME
    su - run a shell or a command as another account

SYNOPSIS
    su [-] [-c command] [name]

DESCRIPTION
    su runs the shell of the account name, root by default, or with -c
    the command through that shell. su is set user id root. A caller other
    than root gives the password of the target account, unless that
    account has none. On a terminal the password is typed without echo.
    Otherwise it is the first line of standard input, read even when the
    account has no password, which lets a program pass it through a pipe
    without knowing whether one is set. After a wrong password su waits
    two seconds and fails with "su: authentication failure".

    Without - the environment is kept, with HOME, SHELL, USER and LOGNAME
    of the account. With - (or -l) su starts a login shell in the home of
    the account with a fresh environment, as login(1) does.

EXAMPLES
    su -c 'pkg install gedit'
    su - anna

SEE ALSO
    login(1), passwd(1), id(1), index(7)
